ING\",\"OFFICIAL\",\"Auto and Truck Manufacturers (TRBC)\",\"Trade / Current Account\",\"International Trade\",\"Inflation\",\"Tariffs\",\"Economic Indicators\",\"Industrial Output\",\"China (PRC)\",\"Purchasing Managers Surveys\",\"Employment / Unemployment\",\"Business Sentiment\",\"Asia / Pacific\",\"Major News\",\"Industrials (TRBC)\",\"Monetary / Fiscal Policy / Policy Makers\",\"Polls\",\"Labour / Personnel\",\"Pictures\",\"Economic News (3rd Party)\",\"Emerging Market Countries\",\"United States\", \"Article\", \"China\"],\n        \"about\":\"Article\"\n    }",
              "# China factory activity shrinks for first time in over two years, 2019 looks tougher\nRyan Woo, Lusha Zhang\n\n5 Min Read\n\nBEIJING (Reuters) - China’s factory activity contracted for the first time in over two years in December, highlighting the challenges facing Beijing as it seeks to end a bruising trade war with Washington and reduce the risk of a sharper economic slowdown in 2019",
